-- title:
--   Covariance of the 2× 3 Fourier transform under transvections
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. a point of the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, write $F = \mathbb{Q}_v$ for the $v$-adic completion, and let $\eta$ be an additive character $F \to \mathbb{C}$. Let $n$ be an integer such that $\eta(x) = 1$ for every $x$ with $\mathrm{v}(x) \le \exp(n)$, and such that there exists $x$ with $\mathrm{v}(x) \le \exp(n+1)$ and $\eta(x) \ne 1$; thus $\eta$ is trivial on the valuation ball of level $n$ but not on the next larger one. Let $\rho : M_{2\times 3}(F) \to \mathbb{C}$ be Schwartz–Bruhat in the sense of the project, namely locally constant with compact support. Let $i \ne j$ be indices in $\{0,1,2\}$, let $c \in F$ and let $X \in M_{2\times 3}(F)$. Here `matFourier23 v η` denotes the threefold iterate `colFourier23 v η 0 ∘ colFourier23 v η 1 ∘ colFourier23 v η 2`, where `colFourier23 v η j` transforms the $j$-th column, sending $\Phi$ to the function $X \mapsto \int_{F\times F} \Phi(\mathrm{setCol23}\,X\,j\,u)\,\eta(u_1 X_{0j} + u_2 X_{1j})$ against the product of the self-dual Haar measure on $F$ with itself. The assertion is that applying this transform to $Y \mapsto \rho(Y \cdot T_{ij}(c))$ and evaluating at $X$ gives the same value as the transform of $\rho$ evaluated at $X \cdot T_{ji}(-c)$, where $T_{ab}(c) = 1 + c E_{ab}$ is `Matrix.transvection a b c`.
--
--   This is the $M_{2\times 3}$ case of the classical covariance of a local Fourier transform under a linear substitution of determinant of absolute value $1$: right translation of the argument by a transvection $T_{ij}(c)$ corresponds, on the Fourier side, to right translation by the inverse transpose $T_{ji}(-c)$, with no modulus factor. It feeds the statement `matFourier23_comp_mul_mul_eq`, which assembles the covariance for general products in the group generated by transvections, as needed for the Godement-section construction in the cubic-induction argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_matFourier23_comp_mul_transvection_eq.lean

